tweets.text:
The AI trade has done more than lift stocks. It's been lifting the spending of the people who own them.

@pboockvar says that's why this sell-off matters beyond markets. If the S&P 500 stays much lower without a quick snapback, he doesn't expect upper-income spending to keep running at the same pace.

"The stock market is the economy, the economy is the stock market."

